1. Definitions
   (a) "Work" means all source code, documentation, prompts, tests,
       configuration, slides, data, run records and other content in this
       repository, including any part, modification or derivative of it.
   (b) "Owner" means Freddy (GitHub: blacktea3250106).
   (c) "Licensee" means any person or organization granted access to the Work
       by invitation or consent of the Owner, including its employees,
       contractors and agents.
   (d) "Evaluation Purpose" means reading, downloading, cloning, building,
       running, testing and internally discussing the Work solely to assess
       the Owner as a job candidate.

2. Limited License
   The Owner grants Licensee a non-exclusive, non-transferable,
   non-sublicensable, revocable license to use the Work solely as necessary
   for the Evaluation Purpose. All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

3. Restrictions
   Without the Owner's prior written consent, Licensee shall not:
   (a) use the Work, in whole or in part, for any purpose other than the
       Evaluation Purpose, including commercial, internal business, product
       development or service purposes;
   (b) incorporate, port, adapt or reuse any part of the Work in any product,
       service, system or codebase;
   (c) create a derivative work that is substantially similar in function
       based on the Work's architecture, flow, prompts, rule design or other
       content;
   (d) distribute, publish, sublicense, rent, lend or otherwise provide the
       Work to any third party other than personnel needed for the Evaluation
       Purpose;
   (e) use the Work to train, fine-tune or evaluate any AI or machine learning
       model;
   (f) remove, obscure or alter any copyright notice or this license.

4. Term and Termination
   This license terminates automatically on the earliest of: (a) the end of
   the evaluation process; (b) 90 days after access was first granted;
   (c) written notice (including email) of revocation by the Owner; or
   (d) any breach of these terms. Upon termination, Licensee shall promptly
   delete all copies of the Work, including backups, and confirm deletion in
   writing upon request.

5. Confidentiality
   Licensee shall keep the Work confidential with no less than the care it
   uses for its own confidential information, and disclose it only to
   personnel with a need to know for the Evaluation Purpose who are bound by
   these terms.

6. No Transfer of Rights
   Access to, review or testing of the Work does not transfer any copyright,
